{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"4218ba29-a3e5-4270-8748-c7b7a0320d16","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have reviewed [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py) (without modifying any existing files) and written the complete findings to [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Key Highlights Covered in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/ANSWER.md)\n1. **Authentication \u0026 OAuth Discovery Traps ([`server.py:148-150`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L148-L150), [`server.py:165-166`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L165-L166), [`server.py:186-187`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L186-L187)):**\n   * `initialize` and `tools/list` succeed anonymously while advertising `resources` capability, so clients that automatically call `resources/list` after startup immediately hit an unexpected HTTP `401`.\n   * `401` responses omit the required `WWW-Authenticate` header (RFC 9728) and return a raw `{\"error\": \"...\"}` object instead of a JSON-RPC error or `isError: true` tool result.\n   * When clients attempt OAuth metadata discovery (`GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` or `/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server`), `do_GET` returns `405 {\"error\": \"use POST\"}` on all paths.\n2. **Streamable HTTP \u0026 JSON-RPC Transport Bugs ([`server.py:135-143`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L135-L143), [`server.py:171-218`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L171-L218)):**\n   * **Hardcoded `2025-06-18` version:** Ignores client `protocolVersion` during `initialize` and ignores the `MCP-Protocol-Version` header.\n   * **Client notifications fail:** Only `notifications/initialized` returns `202`; other standard notifications (`notifications/cancelled`, `notifications/roots/list_changed`, `notifications/progress`) return `200 OK` with a JSON-RPC `-32601` error and `\"id\": null`.\n   * **CORS / Preflight (`OPTIONS`):** No `do_OPTIONS` handler (`501 Unsupported method`), no `Access-Control-*` or `Access-Control-Expose-Headers: Mcp-Session-Id` headers, and no `Origin` validation.\n   * **Batch handling:** JSON-RPC batching was removed in `2025-06-18`, and the batch handler in [`do_POST`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L205-L211) returns `200 []` for notification-only batches, drops `Mcp-Session-Id` generation on batched `initialize`, and embeds raw non-JSON-RPC `{\"error\": ...}` objects inside a `200` array when a batched call hits `401`.\n   * **Session management:** `Mcp-Session-Id` is never stored or validated on the server, and `initialize` reuses a client-supplied header if present.\n3. **Tool Schemas, Error Handling, \u0026 Logic Bugs ([`server.py:25-73`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L25-L73), [`server.py:101-167`](file:///tmp/h-W4J6EU/server.py#L101-L167)):**\n   * **Protocol error vs. tool error:** `get_note` on a missing note ID raises `ValueError` and returns JSON-RPC `-32602` (`Invalid params`) instead of a tool result with `\"isError\": true`, preventing LLMs from gracefully handling missing note IDs.\n   * **Schema mismatches \u0026 unvalidated inputs:** `search_notes` has an incomplete `\"outputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\"}` and returns a JSON array in `content[0].text` vs. an object in `structuredContent`. Incoming tool arguments are not validated against `inputSchema`: missing `title`/`body` in `add_note` raises an unhandled `KeyError` (`500`), `limit: null` in `search_notes` raises `TypeError`, `limit \u003c 0` slices `hits[:-1]`, and `add_note` with `title: \"\"` succeeds but causes strict clients to fail `outputSchema` validation (`minLength: 1`) on subsequent `get_note` calls.\n   * **Resource \u0026 search bugs:** `resources/read` ignores `params.uri` and always returns `notes://guide`. `search_notes` computes the match index `i` on `title + \" \" + body` and uses it to slice `body` directly, offsetting or emptying snippets. `NOTES` is mutated across threads in `ThreadingHTTPServer` without a lock and is never persisted to `notes.json`.\n","duration_seconds":135.83913,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":32351,"output_tokens":7648,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":100582,"total_tokens":39999}}}
